* script to share a folder over the network with cifs on debian, windows serve, linux client:

REPLACE ALL SINGLE QUOTE 'stubs' WITH ACTUAL DATA

==== windows side ====
ITS MANDATORY USER ACCOUNT HAVE DEFINED PASSWORD FOR SHARED FOLDER TO BE ACCESSIBLE
ITS MANDATORY "NETWORK CATEGORY" SET ON "PRIVATE"

select any folder, context menu -> propierties -> sharing -> advanced sharing -> check "share this folder"
advanced sharing -> permissions -> group "everyone" -> "allow all"
security -> user "windows_username" -> "allow all"


==== linux side ====
install cifs:
[CODE]
sudo apt install cifs-utils
[CODE]

write windows credentials:
[CODE]
sudo nano ~/.wincredentials
[CODE]

[CODE]
username=windows_username
password=windows_password
domain=domain_name
[CODE]

give permissions:
[CODE]
sudo chmod 600 ~/.wincredentials
[CODE]

edit fstab:
[CODE]
sudo nano /etc/fstab
[CODE]

add at the end:
[CODE]
#windows-linux shared folder credentials
//'windows_network_ip'/'windows_shared_folder' /home/'user'/Public cifs credentials=/home/'user'/.wincredentials,uid=1000,gid=1000,vers=3.0,noauto,x-systemd.automount,x-systemd.requires=network-online.target,x-systemd.idle-timeout=5s,_netdev,nofail 0 0
[CODE]
